<!-- ── Translator Summary ── -->
<div class="translator-summary">
  <div class="summary-header">✦ Translator's Summary — Hilchos Shabbos 1 ✦</div>
  <p>
    This halacha explains the obligation to eat three meals on Shabbos through the lens of Likutay Moharan I, 60. The core idea: Shabbos is the aspect of <em>yirah</em> (awe), and the eating of the Shabbos meals is what activates this awe — functioning as an "awakening of sleep" that restores the radiant countenance. This is why when Rosh Hashanah falls on Shabbos, the shofar is not blown — the three meals of Shabbos already accomplish what the shofar achieves.
  </p>
  <p>
    The three meals correspond to three spiritual dimensions — <em>Asikah</em>, <em>Z'eir Anpin</em>, and <em>Chakal Tapuchin</em> — and to the three types of awe: awe of the Master (heavenly wisdom), awe of the Talmud (Torah study), and awe of the son (wealth/Kingship). These also parallel the three Patriarchs and the three shofar blasts (TaSHRa"). Through these three meals, one merits the inheritance of Yaakov — boundless wealth. The halacha also connects the <em>neshamah yeseirah</em> (additional soul) of Shabbos to extended breathing, rain, the prayer <em>Nishmas</em>, and the sanctity of Friday night's conjugal union.
  </p>
</div>

